-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",54,{
[1697]="7000B959\n1\tCollect bristly crawler legs (total: 6)\030Collect slimy crawler mandibles (total: 6)\tCrawlers can be found all throughout Tâl Bruinen. Indor has asked you to collect several pieces from the crawlers of Tâl Bruinen so he can have his revenge upon the dwarf who played a trick on him.\n2\tBring crawler legs and mandibles to Indor\tIndor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen. You have collected the crawler bits for which Indor asked and should now bring them to him, so he can add them to the stew he is preparing.\n3\tGrind crawler bits into mush on the grinding stone\tThe grinding stone is near the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth. Indor has asked you to grind the various crawler bits you recovered into mush on a nearby grinding stone.\n4\tBring the crawler mush to Indor\tIndor is at the camp-fire at Echad Candelleth, in Tâl Bruinen. You have ground the crawler pieces you collected into mush and should now bring the mush to Indor so he can add it to the stew.\n5\tBring improved toad stew to Wéthorm\tWéthorm is at Thorenhad, in the Bruinen Gorges of the Trollshaws, north of the bear-dens. Indor has sent you to Wéthorm with his toad stew, and has asked you to pay close attention to the dwarf's reaction to his first bite. Indor wishes to savour his revenge on the dwarf who tricked him into tasting the unpleasant toad stew.\n",
[1698]="7005FFA8\n1\tTravel to Skáilag\tSkáilag can be found to the east of Grúmachath. Rethvárd has informed you that the sorceress, Fláthail, endeavours to raise the Hill-men of Rhudaur at Skáilag. You should travel to Skáilag and defeat Fláthail.\n2\tDefeat Fláthail at Skáilag\tFláthail can be found within the barrows of Skáilag. You have arrived to find Skáilag overrun by wights and other fell things. You should defeat Fláthail.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Fláthail at Skáilag.\n",
[1699]="7005FFA7\n1\tTravel to Toll Oivas\tToll Oivas can be found to the west of Grúmachath. Rethvárd has informed you that the sorcerer, Iärcagar and his pet, Uiagal, lead the Angmarim gathered at Toll Oivas. You should travel to Toll Oivas and defeat Iärcagar and Uiagal.\n2\tDefeat Iärcagar at Toll Oivas\030Defeat Uiagal at Toll Oivas\tIärcagar and Uiagal can be found within the cavern of Toll Oivas. You have arrived to find Toll Oivas overrun by bat-wights and other fell things. You should defeat Iärcagar and Uiagal.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Iärcagar and Uiagal at Toll Oivas.\n",
[1700]="7002EE58\n1\tTalk to Góda in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tLady Góda stands near Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Grief-stricken, Ingbert has asked you to confront Góda about her betrayal.\n2\tTalk to Ingbert in the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tIngbert is in the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should speak with Ingbert about his mother's betrayal.\n",
[1701]="70000039\n1\tBring soft lynx-hides to Old Mugwort\030Collect soft lynx-hides (total: 8)\tLynx prowl through Nain Enidh, east of Weathertop and north of the encampment on the east edge of Minas Eriol. Old Mugwort asked you to collect lynx-hides so he can help Arinora make better blankets for the inn's more affluent guests.\n",
[1702]="7005A56B\n1\tMekhnet has requested that you spend some time with soldiers who are resting around Amdân.\t\n2\tTalk to Mekhnet\tMekhnet sits near the Kambráda encampment in the eastern part of Amdân. She might like to hear about how her fellow soldiers are doing.\n",
[1703]="70028AD3\n1\tDeliver the wood to Urien to complete the shipment\tGaltrev is not far. The wood that you have brought to Fraid at the Galtrev Lumber-camp can surely be carried the rest of the way. You should carry the wood shipment to Galtrev.\n2\tTalk to Urien in Galtrev\tUrien is in Galtrev. You should speak with Urien now that you have delivered the wood successfully.\n",
[1704]="70061365\n1\tCollect wild strawberries (total: 12)\030Collect forest mushrooms (total: 12)\tStrawberries are growing wild along certain paths, and mushrooms are all over the forest bed near Long Cleeve's river. Meregrot North-took has asked you to gather wild strawberries and forest mushrooms.\n2\tReturn to Meregrot\tMeregrot is sitting by the river, south-east of Long Cleeve. You should bring the mushrooms and strawberries to Meregrot.\n3\tPlace the mushrooms and strawberries in the picnic basket\tMeregrot is sitting by the river, south-east of Long Cleeve. Meregrot North-took has asked you to place the mushrooms and strawberries in the picnic basket on the blanket beside her.\n4\tTalk to Meregrot\tMeregrot is sitting by the river south-east of Long Cleeve. You should talk to Meregrot.\n5\tPick up the picnic basket\tThe basket is beside Meregrot, south-east of Long Cleeve. Meregrot North-took has asked you to pick up the picnic basket on the blanket beside her and bring it to her daughter, Rosalinda.\n6\tReturn to Rosalinda\tRosalinda North-took can be found in Long Cleeve. Meregrot has asked you to bring the picnic basket to her daughter Rosalinda.\n",
[1705]="700529CB\n1\tDefeat Skadhurn\tSomewhere in Duskenvale, the massive hart known as Skadhurn protects his herd. You should find and defeat Skadhurn.\n2\tTalk to Goslim\tGoslim can be found in the village Arhaim in Duskenvale. You should bring the antlers to Goslim.\n",
[1706]="7005517A\n1\tDestroy dread-wards in the Circle of Death (total: 4)\tDread-wards can be found in the Circle of Death in Minas Morgul. Faramir has asked you to destroy dread-wards so their magic in the Circle of Death magic might be undone.\n2\tTalk to Faramir at Uialrond, the Dome of Evening\tFaramir can be found outside Uialrond, the Dome of Evening in Minas Morgul. You have destroyed the dread-wards of Minas Morgul and should now return to Faramir.\n",
[1707]="7000370A\n1\tTalk to Cal Sprigley\tCal Sprigley's farm can be found to the south of Bronwe's Folly. Constable Thistlewool has asked you to go to Cal Sprigley's farm and convince Sprigley to bring his family to Archet, where they can be protected from the Blackwolds.\n",
[1708]="70049421\n1\tTalk to Bregdal about Talath Úrui\030Talk to Legolas about Lhingris\tLegolas can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth in Dor Amarth and Bregdal can be found on the border of Dor Amarth and Talath Úrui. When you have completed all you wish to do in Dor Amarth, you should speak to Legolas and Bregdal.\n",
[1709]="70009826\n1\tFind the solution to the riddle\tThe treasure may lie beneath another stone marker, somewhere in Evendim, if this riddle is to be believed: \"High atop Dol Haedír, beyond the Gloaming Falls, Wolf-kin men will guard my last.\" You should examine the marker when you find it for some clue to the location of the treasure.\n",
[1710]="70058C8E\n1\tTravel to Zudramdân\tZudramdân can be found to the north-west of Annâk-khurfu in Elderslade. Glóin has asked you to travel to Zudramdân and rally with one of his scouts, Gárjan. You should travel to Zudramdân.\n2\tTalk to Gárjan at Zudramdân\tGárjan can be found at Zudramdân. You have arrived at Zudramdân and should now speak to Gárjan.\n",
[1711]="7000170D\n1\tSeek out Golodir and Corunir\tThe Rangers Golodir and Corunir are in the Hillman town of Aughaire, a place west of the north exit of the Ram Dúath. Arohir has asked you to seek out the lost Rangers Golodir and Corunir who long ago were sent to Angmar.\n",
[1712]="7004A9E4\n1\tCollect Wose lights\tCollect Wose lights.\n2\tCollect Wose lights (total: 8)\tCollect Wose lights.\n3\tBring the Wose lights to Candúr\tBring the Wose lights to Candúr.\n",
[1713]="7004A9DF\n1\tDefeat Khoshúg the Reeking\tDefeat Khoshúg the Reeking.\n2\tTalk to Candúr\tYou should return to Candúr and apprise him of your efforts.\n",
[1714]="7004A9E0\n1\tDefeat infected Orcs on the path to Bhol Rûdh\tDefeat infected Orcs on the path to Bhol Rûdh.\n2\tDefeat infected Orcs (total: 15)\tDefeat infected Orcs on the path to Bhol Rûdh.\n3\tTalk to Candúr\tTalk to Candúr.\n",
[1715]="70026B0E\n1\tCatch big fish (total: 7)\tFish (both big and small) can be caught at the Fishing Hole in Bywater. You should try to catch many big fish without catching many small fish. Too many small fish will cause your luck to fail! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSpeak with Bollo Bolger\tBollo Bolger is near the Fishing Hole in Bywater. You should speak with Bollo Bolger and show him the large, impressive fish you caught.\n",
[1716]="70007845\n1\tBring Dob Sandheaver his pack\030Collect Dob Sandheaver's Pack\tDob Sandheaver outside the Prancing Pony has asked you to search for his pack at the stone hut deep in the Brandywood, far to the north of Buckland.\n",
[1717]="70008855\n1\tReturn to Taskmaster Ghamp at the Grimwood Lumber-yard\030Collect Grimwood-logs (total: 20)\tFind Grimwood-logs from felled trees or carve them from the Leafcull-trees in the area. Taskmaster Ghamp communicated in his own way that he needs large logs to fix the walls at the Grimwood Lumber-yard.\n",
[1718]="700226C7\n1\tAsk the Gaffer for Bilbo's letter\tThe Gaffer stands outside of his home on Bagshot Row. You should ask the Gaffer if you can show Bilbo's letter to Lobelia.\n2\tBring Bilbo's letter to Lobelia\tLobelia Sackville-Baggins is up at Bag End, north of the Party Tree upon the Hill. You should bring Bilbo's parting letter to Lobelia, for it may give some insight into the locked cellar of Bag End.\n3\tProd Lobelia for information\tLobelia Sackville-Baggins is up at Bag End, north of the Party Tree upon the Hill. You should talk to Lobelia about Bilbo's letter.\n4\tProd Lobelia for information\tLobelia is taking too long to read the letter. You should prod her for information.\n5\tProd Lobelia for information\tLobelia is taking too long to read the letter. You should prod her for information.\n6\tProd Lobelia for information\tLobelia is taking too long to read the letter. You should prod her for information.\n",
[1719]="70015E3B\n1\tPick up the reins to encourage Bill to Follow you\tYou must lead Bill the Pony to safety.\n2\tFind Bill's tracks to find the Wargs that hunt him (total: 6)\tBill can be summoned using the horn you have with you. Bill's tracks can be found on the way to the road, closely monitored by sneaking Wargs. You should find Bill's tracks to draw out and defeat the hunting Wargs. (You may use the summoning horn to call him at any time.)\n3\tTalk to Bill the Pony\tYou have made it to the road with Bill, and he seems to have the willpower to leave the gates of Moria behind now. You should speak with Bill. (You may use the summoning horn to call him at any time.)\n4\tSpeak with an Elf at Echad Dúnann about Bill's passage\tGlavroleth is at Echad Dúnann. You should tell Glavroleth that you led Bill safely to the road.\n",
[1720]="70044E42\n1\tTravel to Bingo's hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tBingo's hobbit-hole is in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.\n2\tTalk to Myrtle Boggs outside Bingo's home in Michel Delving\tMyrtle Boggs stands outside Bingo's home, her arms crossed disapprovingly.\n3\tTalk to Bingo outside his home in Michel Delving\tBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.\n4\tExamine the notice pinned to Bingo's door\tThere is a notice pinned to the door of Bingo's hobbit-hole.\n5\tTalk to Bingo outside his home in Michel Delving\tBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.\n6\tTalk to Donnamira Took in the library of Great Smials and settle Bingo's debt\tDonnamira Took is the librarian in the library of Great Smials, located atop the hill in Tuckborough. Bingo has amassed many overdue fees on the cookbook that began his journey, and he has asked you to settle his debt.\n7\tTalk to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tBingo is inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.\n8\tBoffin Manor has become filled with cobwebs during Bingo's long absence, and he asked you to help him tidy up.\t\n9\tTalk to Bingo inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tBingo is inside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, north of the Town Hole.\n",
[1721]="7004446F\n1\tTalk to Sabert at the east gate of Stangard\tSabert is at the eastern gate of Stangard, the outpost of Rohan along the banks of the Great River. Bingo is reluctant to ride a horse in Rohan, and wants to learn from Sabert whether the kingdom is small enough to experience on foot.\n2\tTalk to Bingo within Stangard\tBingo is in the upper courtyard of Stangard. Sabert has made it clear that walking across the kingdom of Rohan without a horse is not a very good idea, and you should return with that news to Bingo.\n3\tTalk to Bingo in Stangard and walk with him into Rohan\tBingo is in the upper courtyard of Stangard. Bingo is waiting to speak to you and begin the long walk into Rohan.\n4\tBingo is inside the town of Langhold, in the northern area of the Wold in East Rohan. You have entered the kingdom of Rohan with Bingo, and the hobbit wishes to do something for the people of Langhold.\t\n5\tDefeat salamanders in the Wold (total: 6)\030Defeat brigands in the Wold (total: 6)\030Defeat Easterlings in the Wold (total: 6)\tThere are many threats in the Wold of East Rohan that threaten the safety of the people of Langhold: salamanders, brigands, and Easterlings. Bingo wants to help the folk of Langhold by fighting dangerous foes throughout the Wold.\n6\tBingo is inside the town of Langhold, in the northern area of the Wold in East Rohan. You have defeated many threats throughout the Wold to help the people of Langhold.\t\n7\tTalk to Bingo at the entrance to Harwick, in the Wold\tBingo is outside the main entrance to Harwick, on the northern side of the city, in the Wold.\n",
[1722]="700431BA\n1\tShow the dried page of his manuscript to Bingo at the Fanged Pit\tBingo Boffin is at the Fanged Pit. Spalvi has given you the page of manuscript that Willem Whisker found within Moria, and believes that if you show it to Bingo it might help him regain his memory.\n2\tTalk to Spalvi at the Fanged Pit\tSpalvi Stout-heart is at the dwarf-camp near the Fanged Pit.\n3\tTalk to Bói\030Talk to Balk\tSpalvi gave you a number of leads to follow that might help you collect the lost pages of Bingo's manuscript: 'Merrevail in the Fanged Pit might have some pages. Orcs and Warg-riders cover great distances throughout Zelem-melek, and they might have found some pages. A war council was formed in Anazârmekhem, in the Flaming Deeps, and its leaders might have uncovered some pages. Dwarves in the Twenty-first Hall that see a lot of traffic for their services, such as vault-keepers or bards, might also have come into possession of pages.'\n4\tBring the pages of Bingo's manuscript to Spalvi in the Twenty-first Hall\tSpalvi said he would meet you at the Twenty-first Hall after you followed all of his leads.\n5\tBring the assembled manuscript to Bingo in the Twenty-first Hall\tBingo is in the Twenty-first Hall, ready to read the manuscript you assembled.\n6\tWait for Bingo to finish reading the account of his journey\tBingo is reading through his own manuscript... but he doesn't know it!\n7\tTalk to Bingo in the Twenty-first Hall\tBingo is in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria. Bingo has finished reading his manuscript, and you should speak with him to see if it helped him regain his memory.\n8\tTalk to Spalvi in the Twenty-first Hall\030Talk to Willem Whisker in the Twenty-first Hall\tSpalvi and Willem Whisker are in the Twenty-first Hall, waiting to see if Bingo has regained his memories.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in the Twenty-first Hall\tBingo is in the Twenty-first Hall of Moria.\n",
[1723]="70018FCE\n1\tRecover Malbrethil-seeds (total: 6)\tShrews can be found in Taur Hith, particularly in the area around Cerin Brethil, north and slightly east from the Peaceful Glade. Sendiel has asked you to recover seeds from the shrews.\n2\tTalk to Sendiel at the Peaceful Glade\tSendiel is in the Peaceful Glade, south and slightly west of Cerin Brethil. You should return to Sendiel with the seeds.\n",
[1724]="70016BA6\n1\tDestroy nests (total: 6)\030Defeat slingers in Skoiruzg (total: 6)\tThe morroval-camp is located at Skoiruzg, far to the east of the Fanged Pit camp. Gúri asked you to destroy the morroval-perches and defeat several morroval-slingers.\n2\tTalk to Gúri at the Fanged Pit camp\tGúri is at the Fanged Pit camp, far to the west of Skoiruzg. Gúri will be pleased to hear that the morroval-perches have been destroyed and the approach to the camp is free from the attacks of the slingers.\n",
[1725]="70001813\n1\tDefeat Brúni and his falconers\tFalconer Brúni is at Kamskut in the North Downs, north-east of Othrikar. You should defeat Brúni and his falconers.\n2\tDefeat Dourhand Falconers (total: 6)\030Defeat Falconer Brúni\tFalconer Brúni is at Kamskut in the North Downs, north-east of Othrikar. You should defeat Brúni and his falconers.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated Brúni, a Dourhand falconer, and his fellows at Kamskut.\n",
[1726]="70030B9B\n1\tLook for the missing bird towards the west\030Climb the north-eastern ridge\tThe first vantage point can be found by climbing the hill directly east of Oldheart. You should climb the hill and look for the missing bird. This quest requires emotes. You must go to the correct location and perform the emote.\n2\tLook for the missing bird towards the west\030Climb to the western ridge\tThe second vantage point can be found by climbing the ridge further. You should climb further and look for the missing bird. This quest requires emotes. You must go to the correct location and perform the emote.\n3\tTell Oldheart of the fog and the absence of birds\tOldheart stands in his meadow below the great hill, waiting for news. You should return to Oldheart and tell him what you saw from on high.\n",
[1727]="700571AD\n1\tTalk to Léothred elsewhere at Framsburg\tLéothred can be found at Framsburg. You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.\n2\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n3\tContinue learning the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n4\tFind Fram's silver horn\tFramsburg can be found in Misthallow. You should find Fram's silver horn, buried somewhere in the ruins of Framsburg.\n5\tTalk to Léothred at Framsburg\tLéothred can be found at Framsburg. You should talk to Léothred at Framsburg.\n6\tTravel to Hlithseld to rest\tHlithseld is located in the north of Misthallow. You should travel to Hlithseld and rest.\n7\tTalk to Léothred at Hlithseld\tHlithseld is located in the north of Misthallow. You should talk to Léothred at Hlithseld.\n",
[1728]="700303C0\n1\tWisewood the Ent is in the north-east corner of Fangorn's eaves. You should speak with Wisewood once more.\t\n2\tApproach the Huorn who watches you\tA Huorn stands near the White Hand encampment, watching your every move. You should approach the Huorn cautiously.\n",
})
